w: 1.~O Fa- ther, all cre- a- ting, Whose wis- dom, love, and pow'r First bound two lives to- ge- _ ther _ In _ E- den's pri- mal _ hour, To- _ day to these Thy _ child- ren Thy _ ear- liest gifts re- _ new: A _ home by Thee made _ hap- _ py, A _ love by Thee kept _ true. _
w: 2.~O Sa- vior, Guest most boun- teous Of old in Ga- li- lee, Vouch- safe to- day Thy pre- _ sence _ With _ these who call on _ Thee; Their _ store of earth- ly _ glad- ness Trans- _ form to heav'n- ly _ wine, And _ teach them, in the _ tast- _ ing To _ know the gift is _ Thine. _
w: 3.~O Spi- rit of the Fa- ther, Breathe on them from a- bove, So might- y in Thy pure- _ ness, _ So _ ten- der in Thy _ love; That, _ guard- ed by Thy _ pre- sence, From _ sin and strife kept _ free, Their _ lives may own Thy _ gui- _ dance, Their _ hearts be rul'd by _ Thee. _
w: 4.~Ex- cept Thou build it, Fa- ther, The house is built in vain; Ex- cept Thou, Sa- vior, bless _ it, _ The _ joy will turn to _ pain; But _ naught can break the _ un- ion Of _ hearts in Thee made _ one, And _ love Thy Spi- rit _ hal- _ low'd Is _ end- less love be- _ gun. _
